Re-verified today against `main` at `946020d` (2026-09-14): `verl/model_merger/` has had exactly one commit since mid-August, #7610 on Aug 31, and nothing has touched `fsdp_model_merger.py` since. GitHub still reports `e2d9f14` as `MERGEABLE`, so the no-rebase-needed conclusion from my Sep 7 comment still holds a week later. State is `BLOCKED` purely on `action_required` with no workflow ever started.

@wucong25 — sorry to pull you in cold, but you have merged 8 of the last 20 PRs here and this one has been waiting on a workflow approval since Aug 21. Would you be able to approve the run, or point us at whoever owns that? The diff is a single `.clone()` in the `is_replicate()` branch of `_merge_by_placement` plus one CPU regression test, and I verified the red/green locally (reverting just the `.clone()` makes the two merged keys resolve to the same `untyped_storage().data_ptr()`).

I am only a reviewer here so I cannot approve it myself, otherwise I would have already.

